---
import Layout from "../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import BuyBorrowDieCalculator from "../../../components/BuyBorrowDieCalculator.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Buy, Borrow, Die Calculator (United Kingdom) | TaxDebtWealthSuite"
  description="Model the Buy, Borrow, Die strategy in the UK. Compare Lombard Loan borrowing costs vs Capital Gains Tax, check margin call risk, and see your net wealth advantage."
  ogImage="https://taxdebtwealthsuite.com/images/og-buy-borrow-die.png"
>
  <link rel="alternate" hreflang="x-default" href="https://taxdebtwealthsuite.com/buy-borrow-die-calculator/" slot="head" />
  <link rel="alternate" hreflang="en-us" href="https://taxdebtwealthsuite.com/buy-borrow-die-calculator/" slot="head" />
  <link rel="alternate" hreflang="en-gb" href="https://taxdebtwealthsuite.com/buy-borrow-die-calculator/uk/" slot="head" />
  <link rel="alternate" hreflang="en-ca" href="https://taxdebtwealthsuite.com/buy-borrow-die-calculator/canada/" slot="head" />
  <link rel="alternate" hreflang="en-au" href="https://taxdebtwealthsuite.com/buy-borrow-die-calculator/australia/" slot="head" />

  <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline slot="head">
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@graph": [
      {
        "@type": "FinanceApplication",
        "name": "Buy, Borrow, Die Calculator (United Kingdom)",
        "applicationCategory": "FinanceApplication",
        "operatingSystem": "Web",
        "author": { "@id": "https://taxdebtwealthsuite.com/author/#person" },
        "provider": { "@id": "https://taxdebtwealthsuite.com/#organization" },
        "offers": { "@type": "Offer", "price": "0", "priceCurrency": "GBP" },
        "description": "Model the Buy, Borrow, Die strategy in the UK. Compare Lombard Loan borrowing costs vs Capital Gains Tax, check margin call risk, and see your net wealth advantage."
      },
      {
        "@type": "FAQPage",
        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "Is the Buy, Borrow, Die strategy legal?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "@type": "Answer",
              "text": "Yes, borrowing against your own assets is a standard financial practice and does not trigger a taxable event under current tax guidelines."
            }
          },
          {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "How does UK Capital Gains Tax apply when borrowing against shares?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "@type": "Answer",
              "text": "Drawing down funds from a Lombard loan or securities-based line of credit is not a disposal for UK tax purposes, so no Capital Gains Tax is triggered when receiving loan proceeds."
            }
          },
          {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "What happens to asset-backed loans upon death under UK tax law?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "@type": "Answer",
              "text": "Upon death, unrealized capital gains on held assets are wiped out for CGT purposes (Section 62 TCGA 1992), resetting the cost basis for beneficiaries. However, loan liabilities reduce the net estate value for UK Inheritance Tax (IHT) calculations, subject to HMRC debt deduction rules."
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
  </script>

  <main class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12">
    <div class="mb-8 text-center sm:text-left">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-white tracking-tight font-sans">
        Buy, Borrow, Die Calculator (United Kingdom)
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-400 max-w-3xl">
        Model the Buy, Borrow, Die strategy in the UK. Compare Lombard Loan borrowing costs vs Capital Gains Tax, check margin call risk, and see your net wealth advantage.
      </p>
    </div>

    <BuyBorrowDieCalculator defaultCurrency="GBP" />

    <!-- Explanatory Content Wrapper -->
    <div class="mt-12 space-y-8 text-slate-300">
      <!-- Introduction Section -->
      <section class="glass-panel p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-2xl space-y-4">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-[#00F5D4]/10 text-[#00F5D4] text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider border border-[#00F5D4]/20">
          <span>UK Wealth Strategy</span>
        </div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">Introduction</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          In the United Kingdom, the "Buy, Borrow, Die" framework relies on Lombard loans or asset-backed lines of credit to extract tax-free liquidity from growing investment portfolios. Rather than selling shares and triggering UK Capital Gains Tax (CGT) at rates up to 20%, high-net-worth investors borrow against their wealth with private banks while keeping their portfolio fully invested. At death, holding assets until passing allows for a step-up in CGT cost basis under Section 62 of the Taxation of Chargeable Gains Act 1992, eliminating historic capital gains tax for beneficiaries (though Inheritance Tax considerations still apply). This calculator models the financial tradeoff between private bank borrowing costs and immediate UK capital gains tax realization.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Key Benefits Section -->
      <section class="glass-panel p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-2xl space-y-4">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-[#7B61FF]/10 text-[#7B61FF] text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider border border-[#7B61FF]/20">
          <span>Strategic Value</span>
        </div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">Key Benefits</h2>
        <ul class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 pt-2">
          <li class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-[#0A0F1D] border border-[#1E294B] flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="text-[#00F5D4] font-bold mt-0.5">•</span>
            <div>
              <strong class="text-white block mb-1">Compare Lombard Loan Interest vs. UK CGT</strong>
              <span class="text-sm text-slate-400">Evaluate annual private bank lending rates against immediate 10% or 20% UK Capital Gains Tax liabilities.</span>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-[#0A0F1D] border border-[#1E294B] flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="text-[#00F5D4] font-bold mt-0.5">•</span>
            <div>
              <strong class="text-white block mb-1">Model CGT Base Reset at Death</strong>
              <span class="text-sm text-slate-400">Calculate the tax eliminated by holding assets until death under UK CGT base reset rules (TCGA 1992 s62).</span>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-[#0A0F1D] border border-[#1E294B] flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="text-[#00F5D4] font-bold mt-0.5">•</span>
            <div>
              <strong class="text-white block mb-1">Monitor Loan-to-Value (LTV) Risk</strong>
              <span class="text-sm text-slate-400">Track portfolio maintenance margins to avoid margin calls during FTSE and global market contractions.</span>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-[#0A0F1D] border border-[#1E294B] flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="text-[#00F5D4] font-bold mt-0.5">•</span>
            <div>
              <strong class="text-white block mb-1">Preserve Investment Compounding</strong>
              <span class="text-sm text-slate-400">Keep core equity holdings intact in taxable or private bank accounts to maintain long-term capital growth.</span>
            </div>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- FAQ Section -->
      <section class="glass-panel p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-2xl space-y-6">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-[#00F5D4]/10 text-[#00F5D4] text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider border border-[#00F5D4]/20">
          <span>Common Questions</span>
        </div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <div class="rounded-xl bg-[#0A0F1D] border border-[#1E294B] overflow-hidden">
            <button 
              type="button"
              onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('hidden'); this.querySelector('svg').classList.toggle('rotate-180');" 
              class="w-full p-4 sm:p-5 text-left font-semibold text-white flex items-center justify-between gap-4 hover:bg-slate-900/50 transition-colors focus:outline-none"
            >
              <span>Is the Buy, Borrow, Die strategy legal?</span>
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-[#00F5D4] shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path>
              </svg>
            </button>
            <div class="hidden p-4 sm:p-5 pt-0 text-sm text-slate-300 border-t border-[#1E294B]/50 leading-relaxed">
              Yes, borrowing against your own assets is a standard financial practice and does not trigger a taxable event under current tax guidelines.
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="rounded-xl bg-[#0A0F1D] border border-[#1E294B] overflow-hidden">
            <button 
              type="button"
              onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('hidden'); this.querySelector('svg').classList.toggle('rotate-180');" 
              class="w-full p-4 sm:p-5 text-left font-semibold text-white flex items-center justify-between gap-4 hover:bg-slate-900/50 transition-colors focus:outline-none"
            >
              <span>How does UK Capital Gains Tax apply when borrowing against shares?</span>
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-[#00F5D4] shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path>
              </svg>
            </button>
            <div class="hidden p-4 sm:p-5 pt-0 text-sm text-slate-300 border-t border-[#1E294B]/50 leading-relaxed">
              Drawing down funds from a Lombard loan or securities-based line of credit is not a disposal for UK tax purposes, so no Capital Gains Tax is triggered when receiving loan proceeds.
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="rounded-xl bg-[#0A0F1D] border border-[#1E294B] overflow-hidden">
            <button 
              type="button"
              onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('hidden'); this.querySelector('svg').classList.toggle('rotate-180');" 
              class="w-full p-4 sm:p-5 text-left font-semibold text-white flex items-center justify-between gap-4 hover:bg-slate-900/50 transition-colors focus:outline-none"
            >
              <span>What happens to asset-backed loans upon death under UK tax law?</span>
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-[#00F5D4] shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path>
              </svg>
            </button>
            <div class="hidden p-4 sm:p-5 pt-0 text-sm text-slate-300 border-t border-[#1E294B]/50 leading-relaxed">
              Upon death, unrealized capital gains on held assets are wiped out for CGT purposes (Section 62 TCGA 1992), resetting the cost basis for beneficiaries. However, loan liabilities reduce the net estate value for UK Inheritance Tax (IHT) calculations, subject to HMRC debt deduction rules.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Methodology Section -->
      <section class="glass-panel p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-2xl space-y-4">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-[#7B61FF]/10 text-[#7B61FF] text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider border border-[#7B61FF]/20">
          <span>Calculation Logic</span>
        </div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">Methodology</h2>
        <div class="space-y-4 text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          <p>
            This calculator evaluates the net wealth outcome of liquidating UK shareholdings versus securing a private bank Lombard loan. For share liquidations, the model calculates taxable gains by subtracting original acquisition cost basis from market value, applying UK CGT rates (10% for basic rate taxpayers and 20% for higher/additional rate taxpayers) above the annual CGT allowance.
          </p>
          <p>
            For Lombard borrowing, the calculator simulates annual loan drawdowns against pledged securities. It computes compounding interest at private bank reference rates, tracks LTV thresholds against lender liquidation limits, and models the complete elimination of historic CGT upon death under UK tax law.
          </p>
          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-[#0A0F1D] border border-[#1E294B] text-xs text-slate-400 space-y-2">
            <p><strong>Official Reference:</strong> <a href="https://www.gov.uk/capital-gains-tax" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-[#00F5D4] hover:underline font-medium">GOV.UK Capital Gains Tax Rules →</a></p>
            <p class="italic text-slate-500">Calculations are estimates, consult a qualified UK Chartered Tax Adviser (CTA) or FCA-regulated wealth manager before executing private bank borrowing strategies.</p>
          
            <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 mt-3 italic">Reviewed against official HMRC source documents. Last verified: [YYYY-MM-DD].</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Related Calculators Section -->
      <section class="space-y-4 pt-4">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">Related Calculators & Tools</h3>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
          <a href="/capital-gains-tax-calculator/uk/" class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-[#0A0F1D] border border-[#1E294B] hover:border-[#00F5D4]/40 transition-all space-y-2 group">
            <span class="text-xs font-bold text-[#00F5D4] uppercase">UK Tax Planning</span>
            <h4 class="text-base font-bold text-white group-hover:text-[#00F5D4] transition-colors">UK Capital Gains Tax Calculator</h4>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate-400">Calculate HMRC CGT liabilities across basic and higher tax bands.</p>
          </a>
          <a href="/tax-loss-harvesting-calculator/uk/" class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-[#0A0F1D] border border-[#1E294B] hover:border-[#7B61FF]/40 transition-all space-y-2 group">
            <span class="text-xs font-bold text-[#7B61FF] uppercase">UK Tax Optimization</span>
            <h4 class="text-base font-bold text-white group-hover:text-[#7B61FF] transition-colors">UK Tax-Loss Harvesting Calculator</h4>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate-400">Offset UK capital gains using allowable share loss relief.</p>
          </a>
          <a href="/social-security-pension-estimator/uk/" class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-[#0A0F1D] border border-[#1E294B] hover:border-[#00F5D4]/40 transition-all space-y-2 group">
            <span class="text-xs font-bold text-[#00F5D4] uppercase">UK Retirement</span>
            <h4 class="text-base font-bold text-white group-hover:text-[#00F5D4] transition-colors">UK State Pension Estimator</h4>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate-400">Estimate State Pension entitlement based on National Insurance qualifying years.</p>
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
